321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 186 0 R
/T (    The Online Survey System is a web-based application developed in Java to streamline the creation, distribution, and analysis of surveys. Traditional survey processes are often slow and prone to errors, whereas this system automates the entire workflow with modules for user authentication, survey creation, question management, response collection, and data visualization. Administrators can design customizable surveys with various question types, while users can participate easily from any location, improving accessibility and response rates. The system uses Java, JDBC, MySQL, and web technologies to ensure reliability, scalability, and secure data handling. By generating automated analytical insights through charts and summaries, the platform supports better decision-making and significantly reduces manual effort. Overall, the Online Survey System enhances efficiency, accuracy, and usability for organizations, institutions, and researchers conducting surveys)
/E (    The Online Survey System is a web-based application developed in Java to streamline the creation, distribution, and analysis of surveys. Traditional survey processes are often slow and prone to errors, whereas this system automates the entire workflow with modules for user authentication, survey creation, question management, response collection, and data visualization. Administrators can design customizable surveys with various question types, while users can participate easily from any location, improving accessibility and response rates. The system uses Java, JDBC, MySQL, and web technologies to ensure reliability, scalability, and secure data handling. By generating automated analytical insights through charts and summaries, the platform supports better decision-making and significantly reduces manual effort. Overall, the Online Survey System enhances efficiency, accuracy, and usability for organizations, institutions, and researchers conducting surveys)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
