392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (     The primary objective of the Online Survey System is to create a fully automated, user-friendly platform that simplifies the entire process of designing and distributing surveys. Traditional survey methods often involve manual preparation, physical forms, and slow data collection, making them time-consuming and inefficient. This project aims to eliminate these limitations by providing administrators with an easy interface to create customizable questionnaires, manage survey settings, and publish surveys instantly to a wide audience.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (          Another major objective is to improve user participation and data accuracy by allowing respondents to fill out surveys comfortably from any device and location. The system ensures that users can access surveys through a simple and responsive interface, making the process faster and reducing the chances of manual errors. By enabling real-time submission and storing responses securely in a database, the system enhances reliability and ensures that the collected information remains consistent and accurate for analysis.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (2)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (    The scope of the Online Survey System covers the complete digital transformation of the survey process, starting from survey creation to data analysis. The system provides administrators with tools to design surveys with different question types such as multiple choice, short answer, and rating scales. It also includes functionalities for scheduling surveys, setting access permissions, and managing active or closed surveys. By supporting customizable survey formats, the system can be used by educational institutions, companies, researchers, and organizations for various data-collection needs.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
