407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (    The Online Survey System is developed using Java as the core programming language due to its platform independence, strong object-oriented structure, and robust security features. Java provides a stable environment for building scalable web applications and ensures smooth interaction between the client interface and backend logic. Servlets and JSP are commonly used to handle server-side processing, making survey creation, validation, and response handling efficient and reliable.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (     For data storage and management, the system uses MySQL, a widely adopted relational database known for its speed, flexibility, and security. MySQL stores user information, survey questions, and responses in structured tables, allowing quick retrieval and manipulation of data whenever needed. The integration with Java through JDBC \(Java Database Connectivity\) ensures seamless communication between the application and the database, enabling real-time data updates and retrieval throughout the survey workflow.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
