/E (      The login feature allows registered users to authenticate themselves using their credentials. When a user enters their email and password, the system verifies the details against the stored database records using secure validation methods. If the credentials are correct, the user is granted access to their respective dashboard. Administrators are directed to survey management features, while respondents can view and participate in available surveys. This separation ensures that each user interacts only with the functions they are authorized to use.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 201 0 R
/E (    This module also incorporates security mechanisms to protect sensitive data. Passwords are typically encrypted before storage, preventing unauthorized access even if the database is compromised. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
