449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (       The survey conducted for the project generated a variety of quantitative and qualitative responses that helped in understanding user preferences, expectations, and pain points regarding the current system. The collected data included participant demographics, frequency of system usage, challenges faced, and the features they considered most valuable. The responses were organized to identify consistent patterns, such as the common issues users encounter while interacting with existing tools or processes.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
450 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (      To better interpret the collected information, visual insights were created using charts, graphs, and comparative diagrams. Bar charts were used to represent user satisfaction levels, pie charts to display preference distribution, and line graphs to highlight performance trends over time. These visual tools provided a clear and simplified view of the data, making it easier to understand how users behave, what they prioritize, and where system dissatisfaction occurs. Through visual representation, complex data became more accessible and easier to analyze.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
