/Pg 35 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
453 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (      The analysis of the survey responses revealed several important observations that highlight the gaps and limitations in the current system. A significant portion of the users expressed dissatisfaction with the existing workflow, especially pointing out issues such as slow processing time, limited accessibility, and lack of automation. Many participants also mentioned that the current tools they use are either outdated or not user-friendly, which leads to errors, delays, and frustration during daily operations.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
454 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (     Another major finding from the data was the clear demand for improved accuracy and transparency. Users preferred a system that could reduce manual involvement and minimize data entry mistakes. Many respondents emphasized the need for real-time updates, simplified navigation, and better reporting features. The visual insights also showed that users expect customizable options, such as personalized dashboards and quick search functionality, which are currently missing in most existing platforms.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
455 0 obj
<<
