772 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (      The database layer, built using MySQL, is responsible for securely storing all user-related and survey-related data. This includes user login details, survey structures, questions, responses, and report summaries. The database is connected to the application layer through JDBC, enabling smooth and real-time data exchange. The structured storage ensures quick query execution, easy data management, and strong security. Overall, the architecture ensures that the Online Survey System operates efficiently, maintains data integrity, and supports a large number of users simultaneously without performance issues.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K []
>>
endobj
773 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 202 0 R
/E (       The module also includes survey distribution and monitoring functionalities. Once a survey is finalized, administrators can share it with respondents through links or user-access dashboards. Real-time tracking allows administrators to monitor how many users have participated and whether sufficient data has been collected. The system ensures that all updates are reflected instantly in the database, maintaining consistency and accuracy. Overall, the Survey Creation & Management Module provides a complete and efficient solution for designing, organizing, and controlling surveys within the Online Survey System.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K []
>>
endobj
774 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (    After submission, the stored responses can be retrieved and analyzed by the system or by the administrator for further processing. The module ensures that all responses are linked to the correct survey and question IDs, making it easy to organize and filter data when generating reports or visualizations. This structured handling of questions and responses improves efficiency, enhances data accuracy, and supports seamless integration with the analysis module. Overall, the Question & Response Handling Module plays a crucial role in ensuring a smooth and error-free data collection process within the Online Survey System.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K []
>>
endobj
775 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (      Finally, the module allows administrators to export or view reports directly through the system. The report includes detailed summaries, visual analytics, and response statistics, making it suitable for presentations, internal reviews, or academic documentation. Since the data is generated in real-time, administrators can immediately access updated results as soon as respondents submit their surveys. Overall, the Data Analysis & Report Generation Module adds immense value by turning raw data into actionable insights, ensuring that the Online Survey System supports informed and effective decision-making.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K []
>>
